From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: Wine Mono found without a drive for Wine's data directory

In a prefix with no Z: drive the shared Wine Mono (/usr/share/wine/mono) is only reachable as \\?\unix\...; mscoree refused such paths ("no drive letter"), so .NET programs did not start there and every wineboot -u ran appwiz's Wine Mono download dialog and waited for an answer -- for ever on a display nobody watches, as in a prefix update. The \\?\unix\ path is used; Wine Mono runs from it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mscoree/metahost.c b/dlls/mscoree/metahost.c
index 44b8ebe..1d91aa5 100644
--- a/dlls/mscoree/metahost.c
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/metahost.c
@@ -1094,8 +1094,12 @@ static BOOL get_mono_path_dos(const WCHAR *dir, LPWSTR path)
     DWORD len;
     BOOL ret;
 
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MONO_NEEDS_DRIVE
     if (memcmp(dir, unix_prefix, sizeof(unix_prefix)) == 0)
         return FALSE;  /* No drive letter for this directory */
+#endif
+    /* a prefix without a drive for Wine's data directory (no Z:) reaches it as \\?\unix\... */
+    (void)unix_prefix;
 
     len = lstrlenW( dir ) + lstrlenW( basedir ) + 1;
     if (!(dos_dir = malloc( len * sizeof(WCHAR) ))) return FALSE;
